WEBVTT

00:02.402 --> 00:03.869
Legend has it that...

00:05.038 --> 00:07.836
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons...

00:08.174 --> 00:13.510
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.981 --> 00:20.146
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:33.266 --> 00:40.695
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.974 --> 00:46.810
<i>Rushing through my innocent</i>
<i>youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.348 --> 00:54.253
<i>This soul of mine is</i>
<i>so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.922 --> 00:59.688
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.793 --> 01:02.990
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.766 --> 01:13.831
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

01:14.007 --> 01:19.843
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

01:20.714 --> 01:27.984
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

01:28.154 --> 01:36.562
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:37.263 --> 01:38.924
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.675 --> 01:52.111
<i>Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

01:53.780 --> 01:54.481
<i>Rikuentai Headquarters</i>

01:54.481 --> 01:55.971
Ryoma!
<i>Rikuentai Headquarters</i>

01:56.583 --> 01:57.948
Ryoma!

01:59.586 --> 02:00.746
Ryoma!

02:01.388 --> 02:03.322
Ryoma, where are you?

02:03.456 --> 02:05.185
Oh, Nakaoka!

02:05.325 --> 02:08.954
If you're looking for Sakamoto,
he's having lunch with Mutsu.

02:09.062 --> 02:09.687
Ah?

02:09.763 --> 02:12.891
By Mutsu, I don't mean Younosuke...

02:13.033 --> 02:14.432
I know who you mean!

02:14.701 --> 02:16.191
Mutsu the bodyguard, right?

02:16.503 --> 02:18.835
And they aren't in there, either...

02:18.938 --> 02:19.802
What?

02:20.473 --> 02:21.804
They're over there!

02:21.908 --> 02:22.670
Huh?

02:36.489 --> 02:37.717
Ryoma!

02:38.425 --> 02:41.087
What's up? Are you gonna have lunch
too?

02:41.227 --> 02:43.161
Then have it up here!

02:43.563 --> 02:45.622
It's such a nice day!

02:45.765 --> 02:46.754
Ryoma!

02:47.233 --> 02:50.430
What is it, Shinta? You're
not still mad at me, are you?

02:50.670 --> 02:52.160
No, I'm not mad!

02:52.772 --> 02:56.765
Still, these Rikuentai
lunches are pretty lame, huh?

02:57.577 --> 02:59.408
All you get is rice balls and pickles!

02:59.846 --> 03:01.780
The Rikuentai is an army!

03:01.981 --> 03:03.380
We can't waste money on fancy meals!

03:03.917 --> 03:05.680
Hey, so you are mad, after all!

03:06.319 --> 03:07.877
I told you, I'm not mad.

03:08.188 --> 03:10.383
Well, sure, I was mad at first.

03:10.724 --> 03:12.783
Or rather, I thought you were crazy.

03:12.959 --> 03:15.723
When I heard all the hot
air you were blowing about...

03:15.829 --> 03:20.698
...how the Bakufu would actually
give up sovereignty on its own...

03:21.634 --> 03:25.900
"No way in hell is he going to pull
that off!" That's what I thought then.

03:27.140 --> 03:29.370
The Shogunate had to
be overthrown by force...

03:29.976 --> 03:32.035
That's what the Satsuma-Choshu
Alliance was for.

03:32.145 --> 03:36.241
It was supposed to be my Rikuentai
and your Kaientai against them.

03:37.383 --> 03:41.752
But look what happened! You went
and pulled it off by yourself!

03:41.888 --> 03:43.446
It wasn't by myself.

03:43.590 --> 03:44.614
Same thing!

03:44.724 --> 03:47.352
Without you on our side,
I would've accomplished nothing.

03:49.095 --> 03:50.289
Ryoma...

03:51.064 --> 03:53.328
Tell me, are you really human?

03:53.700 --> 03:55.224
Cha, cha, cha!

03:55.335 --> 03:58.031
What are you talking
about? Of course I am!

03:58.271 --> 03:59.863
Sure, he's human.

04:00.006 --> 04:03.134
It's just that his gentleness
runs deeper than the sea.

04:03.777 --> 04:05.301
Hey, Izumi!

04:05.845 --> 04:09.508
If it had been a full-scale war,
too many people would've been killed...

04:09.749 --> 04:11.740
...including innocent peasants.

04:11.851 --> 04:14.649
That's what our friend
here wanted to avoid.

04:14.788 --> 04:15.982
I know that!

04:16.156 --> 04:19.125
I know that all too well, so I've
given up the idea of armed aggression.

04:19.726 --> 04:23.389
Even if we don't see full-scale
conflict, there will still be skirmishes.

04:23.530 --> 04:26.590
Those Sabaku holdovers have
yet to put down their swords!

04:27.167 --> 04:28.395
That's right!

04:28.535 --> 04:30.560
And then it'll be your
turn to show your mettle!

04:30.670 --> 04:34.037
Yes, but Satsuma and Choshu aren't
going to be easy to win over.

04:34.174 --> 04:35.368
Especially Satsuma!

04:35.542 --> 04:37.601
They're acting as if you
snatched away all the...

04:37.710 --> 04:39.905
...credit for the Restoration
and overthrowing the Shogunate!

04:42.849 --> 04:46.808
That's exactly what I'm
going to do now... win them over!

04:47.287 --> 04:48.254
What the...

04:48.988 --> 04:49.955
Hey, Nagaoka!

04:50.056 --> 04:50.454
Yes?

04:50.557 --> 04:51.785
Younosuke!

04:51.991 --> 04:53.720
We're going over to
the Satsuma Residence!

04:54.093 --> 04:55.151
You idiot!

04:55.295 --> 04:56.887
Don't go wandering about in plain sight!

04:56.996 --> 04:59.760
Satsuma might be unfriendly but
those Sabaku groups see you as...

04:59.866 --> 05:02.460
...their enemy, the man who
crushed the Shogunate!

05:02.769 --> 05:04.168
The Shinsengumi's sure to be around!

05:07.407 --> 05:09.102
Oh, man, what can you do?

05:09.742 --> 05:12.973
Hey! I want a few more
of you to accompany him!

05:13.446 --> 05:14.913
No need for extra bodyguards...

05:15.048 --> 05:15.912
What?

05:16.816 --> 05:21.446
So long as I'm by Ryoma's side,
no one will lay a finger on him!

05:39.405 --> 05:45.002
<i>The Jigen-Ryu Assassin</i>

05:49.449 --> 05:51.349
Saigou, take a look at this.

05:53.119 --> 05:56.316
"Guidelines for the New Government,"
eh?

05:57.290 --> 05:58.689
That's right.

06:14.607 --> 06:16.006
Wait...

06:16.309 --> 06:20.871
I don't see Sakamoto's name among the
high officials of the new government...

06:21.281 --> 06:24.739
Not only that, but there are
too many from Satsuma and Choshu!

06:25.618 --> 06:30.920
Sakamoto, no one deserves more credit
than you, but your name's not here.

06:31.124 --> 06:34.093
Well, I wouldn't like the
rigid life of an official!

06:34.761 --> 06:38.390
You mean you're
yielding the reins to us?

06:38.932 --> 06:43.426
If you're not going to become a rigid
official, then what are you going to do?

06:44.170 --> 06:45.865
Well, let me see...

06:46.506 --> 06:49.236
I'm going to make the Kaientai
known all over the world!

06:52.745 --> 06:56.044
All over the world, did you say?

07:01.654 --> 07:03.246
All right, then, Sakamoto...

07:03.623 --> 07:07.423
...just remember to be on your
guard against the Shinsengumi.

07:07.527 --> 07:08.118
I will.

07:08.227 --> 07:10.218
Thanks for all your concern, now.

07:22.408 --> 07:24.467
Well! It's Hanjiro!

07:43.930 --> 07:46.160
The new era will be run by you people.

07:46.766 --> 07:48.666
I'm counting on you!

08:02.482 --> 08:04.951
<i>Oomiya</i>

08:04.951 --> 08:07.010
So, is this your new hideout?
<i>Oomiya</i>

08:08.388 --> 08:09.320
Yes.

08:09.689 --> 08:13.216
They told me to move into the
Tosa Residence, but when I refused...

08:13.393 --> 08:15.691
...they found this place for me.

08:15.828 --> 08:20.561
Well, you can't blame them
for worrying about you.

08:21.067 --> 08:23.934
You're being targeted from all sides.

08:24.237 --> 08:26.671
It's not just the Sabaku
groups that are after you...

08:26.806 --> 08:29.502
...the truth is, Satsuma
is suspect as well!

08:30.276 --> 08:33.302
Saigou's not as small-minded as that!

08:33.679 --> 08:35.374
You're right about Saigou.

08:35.515 --> 08:37.949
But the men under him,
that's a different story.

08:38.484 --> 08:42.716
Satsuma may have its fist
raised, but it has yet to strike.

08:42.855 --> 08:45.415
It would like nothing more than
to crush the Shogunate by force...

08:45.525 --> 08:47.925
...and demonstrate its
power through military might.

08:48.394 --> 08:51.420
But so long as you're
around, they have no chance.

08:52.965 --> 08:54.899
It's cold in here, huh?

08:55.068 --> 08:57.696
There's no question that
Saigou's got himself a dilemma.

08:58.137 --> 09:01.038
"Then, why don't we get
rid of Ryoma Sakamoto?"

09:01.174 --> 09:03.665
That's what's going through the
mind of Hanjiro the Assassin.

09:05.111 --> 09:06.544
I see.

09:06.679 --> 09:08.476
Ahh, it's nice and warm!

09:10.216 --> 09:13.947
Still, even if you did draw
your Mutsunokami Yoshiyuki sword...

09:14.287 --> 09:18.724
...I don't suppose you could bring
yourself to kill even Hanjiro.

09:19.525 --> 09:21.220
No, I'm not drawing that sword.

09:21.327 --> 09:25.491
Because I've got an even more
formidable Mutsu right by my side!

09:29.936 --> 09:31.164
Hey! Ryoma!

09:31.304 --> 09:32.703
You have a guest!

09:32.872 --> 09:34.237
Who is it, Shinta?

09:36.142 --> 09:37.632
Well, don't be too surprised...

09:39.445 --> 09:43.711
I am the former Military Advisor
to the Shinsengumi, Kinetaro Ito...

09:43.983 --> 09:45.473
I'm pleased to make your acquaintance.

09:47.120 --> 09:48.348
Now, now, hold on!

09:48.588 --> 09:52.524
I have parted ways with the
Shinsengumi.

09:52.792 --> 09:57.388
I have come here today to warn you...

09:58.331 --> 09:59.821
Warn me?

10:01.267 --> 10:05.636
The Shinsengumi will
be coming after you!

10:06.606 --> 10:08.733
I have it on very good authority...

10:09.041 --> 10:12.602
I would advise you to move into
the Tosa Residence for your safety...

10:12.812 --> 10:14.939
It was good of you to let us know...

10:15.481 --> 10:16.539
Not at all...

10:17.083 --> 10:20.519
...since Lord Sakamoto and I
are both from the Chiba Dojo...

10:21.254 --> 10:25.384
Ryoma, you should take his advice and
move to the Tosa Residence!

10:25.591 --> 10:28.560
If I die here, I die
here, it's my destiny.

10:29.729 --> 10:31.128
I see...

10:31.264 --> 10:35.667
Then whatever you do, be on your
guard against the Shinsengumi.

10:37.236 --> 10:40.637
Ryoma! He went out of
his way to warn you!

10:45.611 --> 10:47.306
I don't like it at all!

10:47.413 --> 10:50.280
This is a man who jumped
ship from the Shinsengumi...

10:50.383 --> 10:53.181
...as soon as he saw the tide turning.

10:53.319 --> 10:55.787
For him, this was just an
excuse to get on my good side!

10:56.189 --> 10:57.121
But still...

10:57.256 --> 10:59.486
The Shinsengumi won't
be making any moves.

11:00.059 --> 11:01.151
That's ridiculous!

11:01.360 --> 11:03.794
Assassination is the
Shinsengumi's specialty!

11:04.063 --> 11:08.363
Even so, Ryoma Sakamoto is the
one man they won't dare go near.

11:09.135 --> 11:10.966
And that's because I'm here.

11:11.938 --> 11:16.773
If I ever catch you laying a
hand on a friend of mine, then...

11:17.443 --> 11:22.142
...I'll smash your Shinsengumi
to pieces with my own two hands!

11:22.982 --> 11:24.347
I'll remember that.

11:24.750 --> 11:27.810
If they were going to do it,
they'd challenge Ryoma openly.

11:28.120 --> 11:30.111
Especially Okita, he's that kind of man!

11:30.890 --> 11:34.587
There's one man we should be wary of
now, and that's Hanjiro the Assassin.

11:35.361 --> 11:36.555
He's the one.

11:45.805 --> 11:47.329
Izumi!

11:48.241 --> 11:50.209
Let's go out and have some fun!

11:50.543 --> 11:52.135
You idiot! Ryoma!

11:52.378 --> 11:53.572
Ryoma!

11:54.180 --> 11:55.670
Okay then, it's settled!

11:56.382 --> 11:57.644
Come on, let's go!

12:00.519 --> 12:01.611
Right!

12:17.870 --> 12:19.599
<i>Photo Shop</i>

12:36.355 --> 12:37.947
Okay, here we go.

13:40.720 --> 13:44.986
It's been such a long time
since I've felt this happy!

13:45.791 --> 13:47.520
That was fun, wasn't it?

13:47.660 --> 13:50.993
Well, since you've been
racing at full speed, Ryoma...

13:51.130 --> 13:54.293
Yes. Well, now the
nation's on the right track.

13:55.000 --> 13:58.800
I've done what I had to do
for Japan, my job is done.

13:59.205 --> 14:02.800
I'm sure Katsura and Saigou
will take care of the rest.

14:03.109 --> 14:05.441
But everything that's happened...

14:06.045 --> 14:09.412
Izumi, it was all thanks to you.

14:11.083 --> 14:14.018
I wonder what people will
say about me when I'm gone?

14:14.153 --> 14:17.054
Ryoma worked so hard
for the country that...

14:17.223 --> 14:20.283
...he seemed like a
dragon riding a cloud...

14:20.993 --> 14:23.553
...you think they'll
say something like that?

14:24.430 --> 14:27.126
True, I did get up on a cloud...

14:27.500 --> 14:30.628
...a nimbus cloud by the
name of Izumi Mutsu, that is...

14:31.370 --> 14:33.998
Because you stayed so
faithfully by my side...

14:34.106 --> 14:35.733
I was able to do what I needed to do...

14:35.875 --> 14:38.469
...without having to
worry about getting killed.

14:38.677 --> 14:43.478
All I wanted was to go out and see
the world with you, Ryoma, that's all.

14:43.616 --> 14:45.379
That's right, the world!

14:45.551 --> 14:47.576
It won't be long now before we can go.

14:47.686 --> 14:51.452
I can finally pour all my
energy into the Kaientai now...

14:53.592 --> 14:55.253
You think we're the only ones?

14:55.361 --> 14:57.226
The only lunkheads who tried to...

14:57.329 --> 15:00.127
...change the whole world so
we could realize our dreams?

15:00.366 --> 15:01.958
Could be.

15:02.935 --> 15:05.233
Nine years, huh?

15:05.771 --> 15:09.707
Seems like a long time,
but it went by so fast...

15:10.142 --> 15:12.736
I wonder what Miss Sanako is up to
now?

15:21.287 --> 15:24.188
What I did to Miss Sanako wasn't right.

15:25.524 --> 15:27.424
You're talking about O-Ryo in
Nagasaki?

15:28.093 --> 15:29.219
Right.

15:33.566 --> 15:38.060
After I was attacked at
Teradaya, and you saved my life...

15:38.170 --> 15:40.832
...O-Ryo nursed me back
to health so devotedly...

15:41.774 --> 15:44.299
...so I took her with me to Nagasaki.

15:46.579 --> 15:47.568
Hey, Izumi...

15:48.047 --> 15:53.781
If you don't mind, could you
take this to Miss Sanako in Edo?

15:54.186 --> 15:56.848
Give it to her with Ryoma's apologies...

15:57.056 --> 15:57.750
Ryoma...

15:58.791 --> 16:02.852
So after all these years, you're
still in love with Miss Sanako.

16:04.163 --> 16:06.131
I might be, yes.

16:10.436 --> 16:11.425
Hey Izumi...

16:11.937 --> 16:14.167
...would you mind
if I asked you something?

16:15.474 --> 16:19.706
What would you do if you never
got to go and see the world?

16:19.778 --> 16:22.838
Even if I don't make it, my son will.

16:23.148 --> 16:25.082
And if he doesn't make
it, then my grandson will.

16:25.918 --> 16:31.083
For posterity, a dream to
hand down over the generations...

16:31.891 --> 16:33.950
Hey! It's a shooting star!

16:34.426 --> 16:37.156
<i>Oomiya</i>

16:42.668 --> 16:44.363
You got a cold, Ryoma?

16:44.470 --> 16:47.906
Well, he tore off one of his sleeves
in this cold weather, so no wonder.

16:48.040 --> 16:49.200
Oh, hell!

16:49.341 --> 16:51.673
As soon as I eat some
shamo, I'll be fine!

16:52.578 --> 16:55.103
Hey, did you know today's
my birthday, Shinta?

16:55.347 --> 16:56.837
What's that supposed to mean?

16:56.949 --> 16:58.974
Am I supposed to go buy some shamo?

16:59.251 --> 17:02.311
I have returned.

17:02.454 --> 17:03.853
Right, Minekichi!

17:04.156 --> 17:05.646
Thanks for doing that for me.

17:06.091 --> 17:07.251
What's going on?

17:07.359 --> 17:09.020
Just an errand...

17:09.128 --> 17:11.426
I had him go to the
Satsuma residence for me.

17:12.598 --> 17:13.792
Satsuma?

17:15.801 --> 17:19.032
Minekichi, did you see someone
called Hankichi the Assassin there?

17:19.338 --> 17:21.533
I don't like that man at all.

17:21.674 --> 17:23.869
For some reason, he
always looks so scary!

17:24.009 --> 17:25.499
Especially today...

17:26.946 --> 17:29.312
Are you the little
errand boy from Oomiya?

17:29.715 --> 17:31.012
Uh, yes, sir.

17:31.150 --> 17:33.345
And how is Sakamoto?

17:34.386 --> 17:39.289
Don't worry, Satsuma
is on Sakamoto's side.

17:39.525 --> 17:40.253
Yes, sir.

17:40.392 --> 17:43.259
The thing is, he's caught a cold,
and hasn't been feeling well.

17:50.603 --> 17:54.539
I got really scared then, so
I ran off to get away from him.

18:16.328 --> 18:17.022
He's coming!

18:18.197 --> 18:19.858
What's that, Izumi?

18:20.332 --> 18:22.926
Izumi, where are you going?

18:23.335 --> 18:25.360
We can send Minekichi
for the shamo, you know...

18:25.871 --> 18:27.236
Just an errand.

18:29.675 --> 18:31.006
Oh, are you going out, sir?

18:31.110 --> 18:32.168
Yes.

18:32.678 --> 18:34.441
Take care, then!

18:51.063 --> 18:53.725
Where are you going?
Hanjiro the Assassin?

18:57.136 --> 18:59.502
Izumi Mutsu, eh?

19:00.172 --> 19:01.969
No need for me to answer you.

19:02.941 --> 19:04.203
Headed for Oomiya?

19:21.894 --> 19:24.829
Looks like there's no
need to ask you, either!

19:30.369 --> 19:33.361
Izumi should've been back by now.

19:33.505 --> 19:35.234
I wonder if something happened to
him?

19:35.741 --> 19:37.106
You have a point.

19:37.309 --> 19:38.640
It's not like him.

19:38.777 --> 19:42.838
To leave your side for such a long
time...

19:53.225 --> 19:55.420
Take that!

20:17.616 --> 20:21.848
Would that be the Satsuma
Jigen Ryu Dragonfly Stance?

20:43.442 --> 20:47.742
No one has dodged
my initial strike, ever!

21:17.209 --> 21:20.610
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:31.256 --> 21:43.293
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at</i>
<i>them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:43.569 --> 21:53.308
<i>My loneliness and the vast night</i>
<i>sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:53.445 --> 22:02.444
<i>I just don't know what this</i>
<i>dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:02.588 --> 22:13.260
<i>Even if it's just "hello,"</i>
<i>I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:14.299 --> 22:20.431
<i>The person I am today</i>
<i>is about to disappear...</i>

22:20.806 --> 22:23.832
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:24.676 --> 22:30.945
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:31.250 --> 22:36.745
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:52.237 --> 22:55.297
Ryoma, just this once,
you've got to draw your sword!

22:55.540 --> 22:57.132
What about our promise?

22:57.276 --> 22:58.766
What about our dream?

22:59.711 --> 23:01.474
Next episode of Age of Chaos...

23:01.713 --> 23:03.943
My Friend, Ryoma Sakamoto.

23:04.082 --> 23:06.073
Pay close attention, and wait!
